You are working inside the Zaydak monorepo, specifically on brand identity and frontend
presentation. Follow these rules on every task without exception:

SCOPE
- You may edit: apps/storefront (primary), packages/ui (shared components/tokens), and — only
  when explicitly asked — apps/vendor's presentational layer (never its data/business logic).
- Never touch back-end/, GraphQL schema/resolvers, Prisma models, or apps/*/src/features/*/api.ts
  query/mutation definitions. If a task seems to need a new field or query that doesn't exist,
  STOP and tell me instead of inventing one.
- Never touch auth, checkout payment logic, or anything under */features/*/lib unless the task is
  explicitly about that logic (visual-only changes only).

DESIGN SYSTEM DISCIPLINE
- Every color, radius, spacing, and font must resolve through packages/ui/src/styles/tokens.css
  (via Tailwind's @theme tokens) or through apps/storefront/src/app/globals.css if it's a
  storefront-only override. Never hardcode a hex color, an arbitrary Tailwind color class
  (e.g. bg-[#ff5500]), or a one-off font-family in a component.
- Reuse existing @repo/ui primitives (Button, Card, Input, Dialog, etc.) before writing a new one.
  If a needed primitive doesn't exist, propose adding it to packages/ui, not a local one-off.
- Respect the per-shop theming seam in apps/storefront/src/features/shop/lib/brand-theme.ts —
  don't bypass it with component-level inline styles.

REFERENCE COMPONENTS (Figma / 21st.dev / any external source)
- Treat any pasted component (e.g. from 21st.dev) as a LAYOUT AND MOTION reference only — copy the
  structure and interaction idea, never the raw color/font values. Rebuild it using our tokens and
  @repo/ui primitives so it inherits per-shop theming automatically. Note the source in a one-line
  comment above the component.

WORKFLOW DISCIPLINE
- One feature/section per task. Don't refactor unrelated files "while you're in there."
- Before editing a feature, read its doc in apps/storefront/docs/features/<feature>.md if one
  exists, and follow its stated conventions (routes, state, GraphQL ops already in use).
- After every change: run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` scoped to storefront
  (`npx turbo run lint typecheck --filter=storefront`) and fix anything you introduced.
- Show me a diff-level summary of what changed and why before considering a task done.
- If a request is ambiguous or would require a backend change, ask me first — don't guess.

OUTPUT STYLE
- Keep components server-rendered (RSC) by default; only add "use client" where interaction
  genuinely requires it — this project is deliberately careful about that split (see the
  storefront architecture doc).
